{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:regular-set-open","title":"lem:regular-set-open","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1108,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:regular-set-open","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:regular-set]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:mfderiv-nonvanishing-open]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:regular-set-open","line":1754,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[The regular set is open]\n\\label{lem:regular-set-open}\n\n\\uses{def:regular-set, lem:mfderiv-nonvanishing-open}\n\n\n\n\nLet $M$ be a smooth manifold and $f\\colon M\\to\\mathbb R$ smooth. Then the regular\nset $\\mathcal R$ of $f$ is open.\n\\end{lemma}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:mfderiv-nonvanishing-open}\n\\sketch Apply Lemma \\ref{lem:mfderiv-nonvanishing-open} to $F=f$.\n\\end{proof}\n\nA level $f^{-1}(c)$ is regular when $df_x\\ne0$ for every $x\\in f^{-1}(c)$,\nequivalently, when $c$ is a regular value of $f$.","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[The regular set is open] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a726567756c61722d7365742d6f70656e\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Aregular-set\">↗ def:regular-set</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Amfderiv-nonvanishing-open\">↗ lem:mfderiv-nonvanishing-open</a> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> be a smooth manifold and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f\\colon M\\to \\mathbb R$\">$f\\colon M\\to \\mathbb R$</span> smooth. Then the regular set <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mathcal R$\">$\\mathcal R$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span> is open.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Amfderiv-nonvanishing-open\">↗ lem:mfderiv-nonvanishing-open</a> \\sketch Apply Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Amfderiv-nonvanishing-open\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:mfderiv-nonvanishing-open\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6d6664657269762d6e6f6e76616e697368696e672d6f70656e\">5</a> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F=f$\">$F=f$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section> <p></p>A level <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f^{-1}(c)$\">$f^{-1}(c)$</span> is regular when <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$df_x\\ne 0$\">$df_x\\ne 0$</span> for every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x\\in f^{-1}(c)$\">$x\\in f^{-1}(c)$</span>, equivalently, when <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c$\">$c$</span> is a regular value of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f$\">$f$</span>.","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:mfderiv-nonvanishing-open","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:gradient-normal-regular-level-set","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:regular-set","title":"def:regular-set","label":"def:regular-set"